//
// A CLOSURE WRITE TO A CAPTURED `&` SCALAR IS REFUSED (`@FR-L-CapRef` crossed with
// `@FR-L-CapScalar`).  A `&integer` captured by a closure is COPIED at creation (L-CapScalar),
// and "the `&` itself does NOT survive into the closure, so a write that would replace what it
// points AT is REFUSED" (DESIGN_DECISIONS @C115) — the write could not reach the caller.  The
// refusal is measured on a compound write (`n += 1`), the shape loft#1276 answered quietly
// wrong.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: Cannot write to the `&` parameter 'n' from a closure
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the parameter.
// HOLDS: the sharing and copying cells beside it.

fn cr_bump(n: &integer) {
  g = fn() { n += 1; };
  g();
  n = n + 10;
}

fn main() {
  x = 5;
  cr_bump(x);
  assert(x == 16, "unreachable");
}
